  "result": "{\"seen_before\": true, \"matches\": [\"PowerToys#46239\", \"PowerToys#46589\", \"PowerToys#46800\"], \"answer\": \"This autohide request for the Command Palette dock has been reported before. The main ticket is PowerToys#46239 (Dock: Add autohide support). It asks for the dock to collapse and reappear when the mouse hovers at the screen edge, without shrinking the available window space. PowerToys#46589 and PowerToys#46800 were closed as duplicates of it. The tickets don't say the feature has been implemented, so there is no setting you can turn on yet. Upvote PowerToys#46239 and add your use case there, such as a configurable hover delay and a non-interactive overlay for the device info. The comments in that ticket also discuss showing the dock only on the desktop, or only when the mouse nears the edge. The request to restyle the device info graphs isn't covered by those tickets, so you may want to file it separately.\"}",
